    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is implemented and the full test suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe business-day roll-forward for the registration date lived in one place: `ResolveRegistrationDate.service(...)`, which was skipping only Saturdays and Sundays. I extended it to also roll past the fixed public holidays.\n\n`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/ResolveRegistrationDate.java`:\n- Added a `Set<LocalDate> PUBLIC_HOLIDAYS` containing 2026-01-01, 2026-01-26, 2026-04-25, 2026-12-25, 2026-12-28.\n- Extended the existing roll-forward loop so it advances one day whenever the date is a Saturday, Sunday, **or** a listed holiday \u2014 repeating until it reaches a non-holiday weekday. This naturally chains (e.g. a holiday that lands next to a weekend keeps rolling), and it keeps the single-source-of-truth guarantee the class already provides (daily create-limit, stored date, and membership-number year all derive from this one adjusted date).\n- Updated the Javadoc to mention public holidays.\n\nBecause the resolved date is published once as `Out<LocalDate>` and consumed downstream by `@Val`, no other step needed changing.",
